{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.OfModuleAsModule","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OfModuleAsModule","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.SimpleModule.Basic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OfModuleAsModule.isSimpleModule_ofModule_asModule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OfModuleAsModule.isSimpleModule_ofModule_asModule","kind":"instance","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OfModuleAsModule.lean#L59-L69","doc":"**Simplicity transfers across the round-trip.**\n\nIf `M` is a simple `k[G]`-module then so is `(ofModule M).asModule` — which is the form every\n`Representation`-stated theorem asks for. Stated as an `instance` so that\n`specht_exhausts_irreducibles`-shaped hypotheses are discharged by typeclass inference at the\nuse site. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OfModuleAsModule.ofModuleAsModuleEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OfModuleAsModule.ofModuleAsModuleEquiv","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OfModuleAsModule.lean#L46-L57","doc":"**The `ofModule` / `asModule` round-trip is the identity, `k[G]`-linearly.**\n\n`(ofModule M).asModule ≃ₗ[k[G]] M`. The underlying additive equivalence is\n`asModuleEquiv` followed by `RestrictScalars.addEquiv`; `smul_ofModule_asModule` supplies the\n`k[G]`-linearity. ","signatureChunk":0}]}